  "raw_output": "{\n  \"exercis_typ\": \"CEFR Englis_Placement_Test\",\n  \"section_id\": 5,\n  \"section_title\": \"Reading Comprehension\",\n  \"cefr_range\": \"B2-C1\",\n  \"reading_text\": \"\\\\\nIn the heart of London, a new museum has opened its doors to the public. The Museum of Modern Life showcases exhibits that reflect the evolution of human society over the past century. From advancements in technology and communication to changes in social norms and cultural practices, the museum aims to provide an immersive experience for visitors. The architecture of the building itself is as significant as its content; designed by renowned architect Zaha Hadid, it features innovative shapes and modern materials that captivate both art enthusiasts and skeptics alike.\\\\\nThe museum's collection is divided into several thematic sections: \\\\\\\"Technology and Society,\\\\\\\" which explores how technological innovations have shaped our daily lives; \\\\\\\"Cultural Transformation,\\\\\\\" delving into the impact of globalization on traditional cultures; and \\\\\\\"The Future of Life,\\\\\\\" which presents contemporary challenges such as climate change and biotechnology. Each section is accompanied by interactive displays that encourage visitors to engage with the material in a meaningful way.\",\n  \"questions\": [\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 36,\n      \"question\": \"What is the main theme of the Museum of Modern Life?\",\n      \"options\": [\n        \"The history of art in London.\",\n        \"Advancements in technology and communication over the past century.\",\n        \"Cultural traditions around the world.\",\n        \"Global economic trends.\"\n      ],\n      \"answer\": \"B\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 37,\n      \"question\": \"Which of the following has not been mentioned as a topic in the museum's exhibits?\",\n      \"options\": [\n        \"The impact of globalization on traditional cultures.\",\n        \"Challenges related to climate change and biotechnology.\",\n        \"Historical art exhibits from London's past.\",\n        \"Advancements in technology and communication.\"\n      ],\n      \"answer\": \"C\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 38,\n      \"question\": \"What is the name of the architect who designed the museum?\",\n      \"options\": [\n        \"Leonardo da Vinci.\",\n        \"Zaha Hadid.\",\n        \"Renzo Piano.\",\n        \"Frank Gehry.\"\n      ],\n      \"answer\": \"B\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 39,\n      \"question\": \"Which of the following statements is true about the museum's architecture?\",\n      \"options\": [\n        \"The building has traditional shapes and materials.\",\n        \"It features innovative designs inspired by natural forms.\",\n        \"The architecture is based on classical Greek temples.\",\n        \"The building's shape was chosen to resemble a modern cathedral.\"\n      ],\n      \"answer\": \"B\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 40,\n      \"question\": \"What is the purpose of interactive displays in the museum?\",\n      \"options\": [\n        \"To provide visitors with quizzes and games.\",\n        \"To encourage a more immersive experience by allowing interaction with the material.\",\n        \"To distract visitors from the main exhibits.\",\n        \"To offer guided tours and lectures.\"\n      ],\n      \"answer\": \"B\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
